N5008 [basic.lookup.unqual]/1 + [expr.ref]/1: the explicit template
arguments of a member template-id (`r.is_derived<I>()`,
`(*p).template f<I>()`, `p->template f<I>()`) are expressions of the
enclosing postfix-expression, not of the object's class.  They were
type-checked in the object's class scope (entered to resolve the member
name), so an argument naming the CALLER's template parameter `I` found
nothing and the call had no candidates ("found no match for symbol
'is_derived'") -- CBMC's own small_shared_n_way_ptrt::is_derived,
blocking field_sensitivity.cpp and complexity_limiter.cpp in the
dog-food sweep.
